response:
1. A recursive function is one which calls itself. For example, if we have the following code in our program:
int fib(int n) {
if (n == 0 || n == 1) return 1;
else return fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2);
Then the above code would call itself recursively until it reaches the base case, when the function returns the result of the previous call.

