Please see below for a basic implementation of the Naive Bayes algorithm for text classification using the Accord.NET framework in C#, based on the example datasets provided by the Accord team.  This example shows how to compute the conditional probabilities of each word in a sentence given each category, and subsequently utilize these probabilities to classify a new sentence into one of the three categories.  

For training the model, the Accord.NET TextClassification API provides convenient methods for loading and preprocessing text data, as well as computing the conditional probability distributions and selecting the most appropriate model parameters.  For implementing the Naive Bayes classifier, we first apply the CountVectorizer class to transform the dataset into a matrix of word counts, which is essential for the model fitting step.  We then use the NaiveBayes class to create a Naive Bayes classifier and predict the labels of new observations after fitting the model on the labeled dataset.  Here is the full implementation, including sample output:



